r\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554291#post1554291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like how he hates the Sabbat because they believe in God and he's a Norse Pagan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Whoever made the character actually did their homework and that's why I don't consider Svein to be ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T11:50:23-07:00","id":1554294,"title":"","content":"I only got into VTM when they decided to end it and replace it with the New World of Darkness edition. So it will be fairly short.<br /> <br /> Hesha Rudzhe of the Followers of Set. He struck out to me as he didn't come across as bad troupe for the clan. He is intelligent, articulate, charming and does seem to value his servants welfare more than typical elders. He is devoted to his faith and is well balanced skill and discipline wise.<br /> <br /> Aisling Sturbridge. I'm not a big fan of the Tremere clan, but I liked how she was willing to work with other clans and felt the insular nature of the clan was a liability and watched herself as not to become the things she hated about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> De Ruiz of the Lamsbra clan of Dark Ages Iberia. Here you have a clan member that came from humble beginnings and his skills as a spy caught the Shadows attention and the Christian faction of the clan got to him first and embraced and we saw him become one of the dominant movers and shakers for the Iberian branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T14:42:00-07:00","id":1554295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554294#post1554294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aisling Sturbridge. I'm not a big fan of the Tremere clan, but I liked how she was willing to work with other clans and felt the insular nature of the clan was a liability and watched herself as not to become the things she hated about the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always had the idea that Aisling was how a PC would have their character handled by the Council of Seven. They sent her to New York to basically die but being a PC, she's managed to survive long enough against the Sabbat and emerge triumphant that the Elders are willing to give her a spot despite she's pretty much against all of the traditional things they want a typical regent to be (defiant, self-guided, and reasonably humane for an Ancilla, let alone a Tremere Ancilla).<br /> <br /> Even so, once she survived, she would have been in big trouble if not for the fall of Vienna.<br /> <br /> Ironically, she might have been happier with House Carna but decided to choose loyalty at the absolute WORST time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-10T15:07:15-07:00","id":1554296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554271#post1554271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1st Edition</b><br /> Lodin<br /> Modius<br /> Al Capone<br /> Edward Williams<br /> Duke<br /> Tyler<br /> Thrasher<br /> Helena<br /> Caiaphas Smith<br /> Sullivan Dane<br /> William Shepard<br /> Jacob Prestor/Louis Pasteur</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I think Lodin remains the perfect Prince for a city because he's a guy who could easily be played as either a patron or an antagonist or both. Lodin is evil, at least that's my perspective, and oppressive and an enemy of Anarchs but he's not &quot;ridiculously&quot; evil. He's evil like a Mob Boss but this is a GTA-esque game so to speak. I think there's a lot of nuances to his character that other characters don't get.<br /> <br /> 2. Modius is also a great starter villain and theoretically the PCs as a coterie could overthrow him and take Gary for their own if they wanted. However, do they really WANT Gary? Is it better to be a vampire in Chicago or Lord of a Smaller Land? I felt that was an interesting idea. I also like the 5th Edition update that reveals the powdered wig and effete nobleman thing is an affection. He's actually a lumberjack playing Toreador.<br /> <br /> 3. Al Capone is a character that I think represents kind of the apotheosis of the struggles V:TM went through. Basically, he's a silly character but he's a fun silly character. If you don't want silly in your games, he's terrible, but if you do then he's a great example of the kind of person who might get embraced.<br /> <br /> 4. Tyler is a character I think worked as the perfect Brujah sellout. The character who was once a huge rebel and then became an enemy of it. I find it kind of funny, though, that she's become such a foundational character to the rest of the line, Dark Ages, and tRansylvania Chronicles while everyone else was forgotten.<br /> <br /> 5. Helena is basically Lodin writ-large. I think we're meant to side with Menele (Humanity 10!) over her but plenty of players did her instead because she was pretty sympathetic despite her worst actions. The one in 5th Edition is one I feel is pretty doomed by her present downward trajectory, though.<br /> <br /> 6. Love Caiaphas Smith as a Solomon Kane homage, which is ironic because Sullivan Dane was too.<br /> <br /> 7. William Shepard actually was one of the stars of my novel that I pitched to White Wolf starring Lucita. He became one of the Regional Directors of FIRSTLIGHT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2nd Edition</b><br /> Samuel Haight<br /> Marcus Vitel<br /> Lucita de Aragon<br /> Creamy Jade<br /> The Rose<br /> Michael<br /> Tiamat<br /> The Count/Bela Lugosi<br /> Ezekiel </div> </div> </div>1. Samuel Haight is a character I feel like gets undermined because it was a joke behind the scenes. They had a good premise for the idea of a fake Garou who skinned others. Maybe even the necklace that makes him immortal. However, then they kept making him a ghoul and Thaumaturge and later the whole Baali thing.<br /> <br /> 2. Marcus Vitel is great and I'm glad that they brought him back as the Emperor of Washington DC. Still, he is like Al Capone in that you have to accept the ridiculous to go with the awesome. I regret that they kept Monica Black dead, though.<br /> <br /> 3. I fully accept Bela is the original Bela Lugosi rather than just an impersonator. He also showed up in my other book pitch (which was Theo Bell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Revised Edition</b><br /> Maximilian Strauss<br /> Christof Romuald<br /> Pisha<br /> Heather Poe<br /> Isaac Abrams<br /> Velvet Velour </div> </div> </div>Props to all of the video game creations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>V20</b><br /> Svein Fortinbras<br /> Maria DiMatto<br /> <br /> <b>V5</b><br /> <br /> Arthur Caldwell (I hate everyone else in V5 though, but Arthur Caldwell gets a pass) </div> </div> </div>1. Svein works well because he's very much a Setite without being an Egyptian stereotype.<br /> <br /> 2. Arthur is my favorite creation of what I got to contribute to OPP's Kickstarters (mind you, OPP made everything I submitted so much better).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T17:36:00-07:00","id":1554354,"title":"","content":"I could go along with Aisling Sturbridge staying loyal to the older parts of the clan out a sense of security instead of a possibility of a scary future about the clan's direction. I agree that she would be happier with the Carna faction.<br /> <br /> Maybe she thinks that House Carna is on burrowed time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T05:36:00-07:00","id":1554359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554354#post1554354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could go along with Aisling Sturbridge staying loyal to the older parts of the clan out a sense of security instead of a possibility of a scary future about the clan's direction. I agree that she would be happier with the Carna faction.<br /> <br /> Maybe she thinks that House Carna is on burrowed time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also possible Carna thinks Sturbridge would be a rival or vice versa.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, House Carna is still composed of vampires.<br /> <br /> In my home games, the answer was more...complex. The reason Ailsing Sturbirdge was 100% against joining House Carna and actually supporting their destruction (which fits with Coteries of New York) was that Ailsing was aware of what the <i>Book of the Grave</i> War REALLY did. It was written by a 12th century Malkavian and possesses vast powers that can undo things like the Blood Bond and Kindred domination. What does that sound like? Well, it sounds like the Vinculum that required the magic of Kupala. It also occurred to me, &quot;Who is a 12th century Malkavian that has vast occult knowledge and power?&quot;<br /> <br /> Harold Zettler the Diabolist.<br /> <br /> Now its implied Jacob the Methuselah might be the author but I like the idea that Ailsing knows the entirety of the House Carna deck of cards is based on infernalism.<br /> <br /> (I also have kupala as a female demon in my games because that's the Slavid myth)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T06:38:21-07:00","id":1554360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554359#post1554359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it sounds like the Vinculum that required the magic of Kupala. It also occurred to me, &quot;Who is a 12th century Malkavian that has vast occult knowledge and power?&quot;<br /> <br /> Harold Zettler the Diabolist.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!<br /> <br /> But I would go with the too on the nose obvious suspect<br /> Octavio, the &quot;Voice of Kupala&quot;<br /> He spent centuries warning others of the coming of the signs of Gehenna<br /> And as a bonus as mortal, he was a shaman who somehow touched upon Kupala's dark heart and became suffused with madness.. - so basically he is/was a honorary Koldun and the Vinculum? Based on Koldunic pratices, designed and refined later by Kolduns<br /> he is originally from the area where the Romand built Aquincum and later made his home in Budapest, Hungary where he lived untill 1710<br /> Now the Book of the Grave-War was <i>supposedly</i> written by a German Malkavian in the 12th or 13th century concerning Gehenna and diablerie<br /> Also a large part of what is now Germany was the core and largest territory of the Holy Roman Empire and relations between the Holy Roman Empire and the Kingdom of Hungary were complex, marked by periods of conflict, shifting alliances, and diplomatic maneuvering. For fun, Gertrude of Merania (the Duchy of Merania was a fiefdom of the Holy Roman Empire from 1152 until 1248, he Duchy of Merania had lands that were connected to what is now Germany, specifically the Holy Roman Empire, which included much of modern-day Germany) became Queen consort of Hungary in 1205, married to King Andrew II.<br /> So one could say Octavio was &quot;German Malkavian&quot; in a sense - but this suppsosed author nationality quickly fall apart if you take the book was penned by the ancient Jacob under the guidance of a vampire &quot;more adept in manipulation and control than any other&quot; and Jacob was enslaved by Arabs while a teenager (around 750 CE), and he grew up in Muslim lands<br /> <br /> Sorry for the tangent, it is an awesome ide to use Harold Zettler the Diabolist!\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T08:03:14-07:00","id":1554374,"title":"","content":"Much as Bela the Malkavian amuses me - and he really, really does because \u2018The poor old man not only thinks he\u2019s a Dracula, he really IS Movie Dracula\u2019 is the perfect excuse for some WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS: LA FREE STATES mischief and mayhem - there\u2019s only one sensible answer.<br /> <br /> SULLIVAN DANE, the Old World of Darkness\u2019 very own Peter Cushing (I always wanted to be Van Helsing, not Dracula, which is why I find it so deeply odd that I\u2019ve paid so much attention to this part of the forums).<br /> <br /> Oh, and honourable mention to Arctos the NYC Mage who (At least in THE HUNTERS HUNTED) gives strong \u2018Anywhere but the World of Darkness this dude would be Sorceror Supreme\u2019 vibes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T14:40:05-07:00","id":1554382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554259-your-favorite-v-tm-characters-by-edition?p=1554374#post1554374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Much as Bela the Malkavian amuses me - and he really, really does because \u2018The poor old man not only thinks he\u2019s a Dracula, he really IS Movie Dracula\u2019 is the perfect excuse for some WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS: LA FREE STATES mischief and mayhem - there\u2019s only one sensible answer.<br /> <br /> SULLIVAN DANE, the Old World of Darkness\u2019 very own Peter Cushing (I always wanted to be Van Helsing, not Dracula, which is why I find it so deeply odd that I\u2019ve paid so much attention to this part of the forums).<br /> <br /> Oh, and honourable mention to Arctos the NYC Mage who (At least in THE HUNTERS HUNTED) gives strong \u2018Anywhere but the World of Darkness this dude would be Sorceror Supreme\u2019 vibes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved him showing up in the Red List OPP book because they were masters of those kinds of call backs. The funny thing, though, you had to wonder WHO the guy pissed off so much that the Justicar submitted him to the Illuminati's kill list.<br /> <br /> Because some Red Listers are existential threats to Kindred society. Others are just someone that the Justicar is like, &quot;Finally, I have the authority to fuck up this guy I have hated since forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> In Arctos' case, we don't even know if he's a True Mage or just a Hedge Mage who chooses to live like Stephen Strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T16:54:45-07:00","id":1554384,"title":"","content":"1st:<br /> <br /> Honestly my entry here is a technicality because I like the fleshing out they further get as time goes by, but.<br /> <br /> Menele<br /> <br /> (Some of this is owed to a sequence from revised where before it got ditched as a plot, you realize Menele has actually learned and grew and is trying to walk his talk. What is his ultimate masterstroke against Helena and her line? Not to kill them, not some personal heinous revenge, not some staggering brutality he rationalizes as for the greater good. To just bloodlessly knock them all into torpor so he can try to move on with his unlife. He doesn't want anything from this fight anymore but to extricate himself from it. That's the exact kind of 'defeat my enemy' master plan a high humanity ancient vampire should be busting out. &quot;Nope. Nope, just torpor, not even 'technically someone else will kill you, leaving my hands clean', just torpor&quot;. Earlier editions Menele very much suffers from failed execution in his writing for what he's supposed to be, or certainly what I think the intent with him was compared to how he comes off in practice, but that one side plot arc brought everything together for me for what the idea of him should be)<br /> <br /> 2nd (including Dark Ages 1e as it were, I suppose):<br /> <br /> Michael<br /> <br /> Belisarius<br /> <br /> Thomas Feroux<br /> <br /> Elieser de Polanco (What can I tell you, I like almost all the 'so fucking help me, we are going to be professional, and we are going to be dignified. Oh, just me? None of you are capable of that for ten seconds and it's just going to be me? Well I'm still going to be that way' types. Particularly when they are completely self aware of the world they live in is not and will never be any of those things, or even rewards being those things, but fuck it anyway.)<br /> <br /> Vladimir Rustovich (Someone who is thrilled by the idea that werewolves kinda sorta reincarnate or at least have immortal souls because it means he can get revenge *forever* is doing Dark Ages Tzimisce correctly)<br /> <br /> Mithras (this has as much to do with Victorian Age Vampire, Dark Ages Vampire, and some revised stuff as well, but this is the edition where he gets going really, so)<br /> <br /> Anna Comnena. No she gets basically no screen time or personality to speak of, but the Alexiad is one of my favourite works that I regularly re-read and so she doesn't need it, I know her voice. And Vampire Anna Comnena is such an awesome fucking idea that I love her for her potential, even if it was never realized ;p Honestly kind of art imitating life a lil bit! (At least, obviously, in her opinion *cough*)<br /> <br /> The Order of Bitter Ashes. Not any one specific person from it, I just loved the idea, imagery, vibes and eventual tragedy.<br /> <br /> Revised/Dark Ages Vampire/Victorian/Etc:<br /> <br /> Antara<br /> <br /> Polonia (yes yes, he's from 2nd, but he comes into his own as an interesting guy in revised such that I feel later editions completely waste him)<br /> <br /> Esclarmonde the Black (I have a thing for almost all the vampires that try with clear eyes to build a praxis based on good ideas and on sheer personal competence come *this* close to pulling it off, before getting completely fucking torn down by other vampires due to their own shittiness. Because the problem with vampires is, you know, they're vampires. To paraphrase Margin Call, one of the most vampire movies that ever vampired without actually having vampires in it, you can build that extremely useful and sensible bridge as a huge success, some people will still <i>demand</i> to take the stupid way around anyway)<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly no one exclusive to V20 or V5 made much of an impression on me, and it felt like either edition often dropped the ball with various pre existing characters.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm being super fair to V20 there though, part of its whole thing was de-emphasizing individual narratives until the very end of the line, I can't really blame it for doing its thing, it just felt less dynamic that way. But it was trying to be less dynamic by intent, until the end there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  spacing 10-17-2025, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T21:06:12-07:00","id":1554385,"title":"","content":"I think V20 primarily managed to make it's most interesting character beats in the Children of the Revolution and Dread Names, Dread List for the NPC write-ups. V20 wasn't very NPC focused but they certainly managed to make quite a few memorable ones. Beckett's Jyhad Diary also had a bunch of fascinating takes on the Signatrue Characters that I don't think really got a chance to shine but had a lot of ideas that I liked in their updates:<br /> <br /> * Marcus Vitel becoming Emperor of Washington DC by being a populist anarch leader ala Caesar. It turned out that most Anarchs didn't give a shit about a dictator as long as they got theirs.<br /> * Vykos having been warped by having the Dracon's soul in their brain for centuries and finally getting it out.<br /> * Lucita having a &quot;sister&quot; who is the head of the Sabbat Inquisition (which had been ignored because they wanted to get rid of the diabolism subplot throughout Revised).<br /> * Lucita being set up as the next Sabbat Regent and regaining at least some of her sanity.<br /> * Isabela Giovanni falling into the Setite's hands.<br /> * Ramona joining the Anarchs (who could have seen that coming!)<br /> * Hesha finally coming close to getting the Eye of Hazimel and having no real idea of what to do with it now that he has caught the car.<br /> * Critias as Prince of Chicago because being &quot;first among the Primogen&quot; IS basically the job.<br /> <br /> As for 5th Edition, I am biased to OPP (shocking) but I don't think it ever got any better than Chicago by Night, Children of the Blood, and Let the Streets Run Red.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-16-2025, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T03:30:20-07:00","id":1554411,"title":"","content":"I think the only sensible answer to that is \u2018Whichever makes your PCs life more interesting\u2019.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T15:19:56-07:00","id":1554433,"title":"","content":"1st ed:<br /> - Mithras<br /> <br /> 2nd ed:<br /> - most of the Montreal by Night Cainites<br /> <br /> Dark Ages:<br /> - all of Constantinople by Night Cainites<br /> <br /> Revised:<br /> - Lucita<br /> - Sascha Vykos<br /> - Andrew Emory<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Revised:<br /> - everyone<br /> <br /> V20:<br /> - Dastur Anosh<br /> <br /> V5:<br /> - Julia Sowinski<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T22:48:36-07:00","id":1554509,"title":"","content":"Another character that I liked from the Children of Night write up is Ambrigino Giovanni. He maybe a illegitimate son of Augustus but he didn't let that deter him from learning much about necromancy that he had few peers and fewer that exceed him. I can see Lady Constancia embraced him and I wouldn't be to surprised if she saw as a more deserving candidate of being a direct Childe of Cappadocius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T00:06:35-07:00","id":1554513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/